 that the demon king  was a stubborn  and resilient villain and that he is  willing to destroy both of his sons for  his  own selfish ends this second part of the  arc also gave us the single biggest and  most heartbreaking  death in the entire series the death  of big daddy sunshine our boy  escanor in terms of eskanor's role in  this arc and his eventual death  i have mixed feelings on the one hand  this arc provided a lot of character  development for escondur  and his ultimate sacrifice really  cemented the physical and spiritual  chadliness of big daddy sunshine i mean  even before he got sunshine back from  mael  escanor in his weak human form risked  his life to protect the holy knights  from one of the camara endura seeds  this scene shows us that even without  sunshine escanor  is a true hero he didn't need this  incredible power to be brave and to risk  his life to protect his friends  even in his seemingly weak and squeamish  human form  escanor is still a chad in this scene  eskner also mentions that even in his  sunshine form he still feels  pain and he says that when he fought  meliodus he felt an immeasurable amount  of pain  it was so painful that it nearly killed  him  this revelation allows us to appreciate  escanor  even more when he was in his daytime  form eskanor  always seemed so cocky and  indestructible  but in reality the power of sunshine did  not make him immune to pain  in fact he suffered tremendous pain  especially during his fight with  meliotis  but he was able to withstand it because  of his unbelievable determination  and resilience if anything this makes me  respect escanor  even more but as impressed as i was with  eskanor at this point in the story  i was equally disappointed in my l after  being the badass villain of an entire  arc  and after proving himself to be one of  the strongest characters in the entire  series  mael completely chickens out when it  comes time to fight the demon king  he agrees to give the power of sunshine  back to escanor so that escanor can go  and fight  but mael himself refuses to take part in  the fight because he says that the demon  king is just too  strong really man really now i totally  get that the plot  needed escanor to get sunshine back so  nakaba had to come up with some reason  as to why eskanor is going to be using  sunshine instead of mael  but come on there had to be a better way  to make this  happen they didn't have to do miles so  dirty and make him look like a total  wuss bag  this one brief scene really destroys our  image of mile as a character  and that is why it bugs me so much but  at the end of the day mile is not one of  the main characters so  let's move on when esquinor ultimately  sacrifices himself  in the fight against the demon king and  dies as a result of overusing sunshine  and  overwhelming his body it is truly a  heartbreaking moment  eschanor's sacrifice really brought home  how strong the bond between the seven  deadly sins is  and how unbreakable their friendship has  become the merlin kiss  at the very end of escanor's life was  also absolutely amazing  and it was as beautiful as it was tragic  eskanor's death  really added a lot of maturity to the  story even though the vast majority of  us  wanted to see eskanor and merlin get  together and have a happy ending  it definitely sucks that so many other  characters who were supposed to be dead  came back to life from important  characters like elaine and  arthur to completely unimportant  characters like veronica and freaking  vivian and yet big daddy sunshine  himself  had to be one of the few characters who  died for real  i know that a lot of people wanted  escondar to somehow come back like so  many other seven deadly sins characters  but as much as it hurts us and as much  as we would definitely trade someone  like vivian for escanor  the fact that esquinor really died added  maturity and seriousness to the story  and that has its own value overall i was  still okay with the manga  up to this point and even though it was  hard to cope with eskanor's death  i accepted it as a necessary development  that made the story  more mature for me the real issues begin  once we get to the final major arc in  the story the king  of chaos arc this arc takes place right  after the defeat of the demon king  and the death of escanor merlin the only  sin  whose true motivations had not yet been  fully revealed  transports the sins back to lake  salisbury  there she brings king arthur back from  the dead  and resurrects him as the king of chaos  i don't have a problem with the arc up  to this point the seven deadly sins is  heavily inspired by arthurian legend  and so bringing king arthur back to life  makes a lot of sense  in fact i thought that chaos power was  actually really  cool and it had been foreshadowed  earlier on in the story so again  all of this made sense to me i even  liked the inclusion of the lady of the  lake  a magical being brought from chaos that  we met in the previous arc  the lady of the lake plays a significant  role in arthurian legend  so again all good up to this point but  then we arrive at the first  big issue with this arc and that is  merlin and her true motivations  the lady of the lake reveals that merlin  has been hiding the truth about chaos  power from the sins for this  entire time that is because as a child  merlin  fell in love with meliotis because he  had saved her from the wizards of bel  alwyn who only wanted to experiment on  her and use her for her magical talents  because meliotis was the only one who  saw her as a person  and not just as some magical tool merlin  fell hopelessly in love with meliotis  but as we all know meliotis was already  in love with elizabeth  so merlin realized that she could never  stand a chance with meliotis  in order to fill this empty void in her  heart  she dedicated her entire life to one  purpose  resurrecting the power of chaos and this  is an ancient power that had been sealed  away by the demon king  and the supreme deity in pursuit of this  goal merlin was even willing to betray  the seven deadly sins such as when she  decided to reactivate  elizabeth's curse and this part about  merlin and her true motivations  really rubbed me the wrong way are you  really going to tell me that this  mysterious and epically cool  female wizard did everything she did for  the past 3000 years just because she  needed to fill a void in her heart  left by her unrequited love for meliotis  i mean really  meliotis is already loved by elizabeth  and zanery  and diane was into him for years before  she finally fell for king  so did we really need a fourth woman in  the story to be in love with meliotis  don't get me wrong i would totally get  it if merlin fell in love with him back  when she first met him because he saved  her  and treated her as an actual person  instead of some magical experiment  but for her to stay in love with him for  over 3000  years knowing that he is meant to be  with elizabeth just rubs me the wrong  way  now we all know that love is crazy and  you can't choose who you fall in love  with and all of that stuff  but still i would have been so much  happier if merlin could have just gotten  over meliodas  just like the end did so that merlin  could finally give eskanor a chance  and that whole thing about merlin  pursuing chaos power  just as some sort of distraction from  her love for meliotis  and then her being willing to even  potentially put her friends in danger  in the pursuit of that goal i don't know  it just doesn't quite fit  to me now if there had been some bigger  reason like say if chaos power was the  only thing that could defeat the supreme  deity  then i could see merlin pursuing it  because she knows that eventually they  will have to take on the supreme deity  but  this whole idea of pursuing chaos just  out of curiosity or just as a  distraction from a broken heart  i didn't like it and speaking of the 