g who was the problem  and his defeat on its own doesn't solve  all of britannia's issues  if anything now that the balance of  power has been disrupted  the supreme deity could be more  dangerous than ever  and yet the story seemed to completely  ignore the supreme deity  and the celestial realm and after the  cath palug fight  the manga ended we got those final few  chapters after the time skips which i  actually liked quite a bit  but that chaos arc really felt rushed  and  incomplete merlin's true intentions the  supreme deity  chaos power and the lady of the lake and  her role in the whole story  all of these aspects of the story felt  incomplete when the manga ended  also how are they gonna do that to hawks  mama she just gets consumed by arthur  and disappears from the story  after everything she did for the sins  not cool man  not cool now it is possible that the  sequel manga is planning to cover the  supreme deity and that is why we didn't  get to see her in the original manga  and from the lancelot side story it is  clear that the lady of the lake  is definitely going to be relevant to  the sequel so maybe the same will be the  case  for the supreme deity if that's true  then fine  but that doesn't change the fact that  the original manga ended with  kath as the final major villain and that  was just  underwhelming in my opinion so for me  personally the biggest  issues with the ending were merlin's  true intentions and her flimsy  justifications for wanting to resurrect  chaos even at the cost of putting her  friends in danger  and the ignoring of the supreme deity  while elevating a side character like  kath palug into the final villain in the  story  if i could change the story in any way  that i wanted i definitely would have  expanded the chaos arc  included an epic final battle against  the supreme deity  and i would have fleshed out merlin's  true intentions more thoroughly  but those are just my own thoughts on  the ending and i've been thinking a