eity and  hsk points out that it would have been  cool to see the celestial realm  and to learn more about hawk's mama i  have to agree on these points as well  we might still get more about this stuff  in the sequel but i think it would have  been better to include it in the main  story  over on instagram we also had a number  of comments saying that the supreme  deity should have been the final villain  like this one from luffy king 355 we had  multiple comments saying that esquinor  should not have died or that he should  have been revived  such as these comments by taki xtaki  benny reds and  nate nightingale there were also some  comments like this one by lame head park  beth about the possibility of the  supreme deity being involved  in the sequel and i think that's  definitely possible  but i still agree with the people who  wanted to see the supreme deity as the  final villain in the original story  nevertheless i am excited for the sequel  and i will definitely give it a chance  huge thanks to everyone who gave their  input on twitter and instagram  and feel free to let me know what you  guys think down in the comments below  how do you guys think that the seven  deadly sins manga should have ended  were there any issues that particularly  rubbed you the wrong way  and what would you like to see in the  sequel let me know  down below if you enjoyed this video and  you want to see more seven deadly synths  content and sequel content right here on  the channel  please leave a like to let me know it  really does help and if you happen to be  new to anime opera  or maybe you just haven't subscribed  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on all notifications  as always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time  see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you

