g who was the problem  and his defeat on its own doesn't solve  all of britannia's issues  if anything now that the balance of  power has been disrupted  the supreme deity could be more  dangerous than ever  and yet the story seemed to completely  ignore the supreme deity  and the celestial realm and after the  cath palug fight  the manga ended we got those final few  chapters after the time skips which i  actually liked quite a bit  but that chaos arc really felt rushed  and  incomplete merlin's true intentions the  supreme deity  chaos power and the lady of the lake and  her role in the whole story  all of these aspects of the story felt  incomplete when the manga ended  also how are they gonna do that to hawks  mama she just gets consumed by arthur  and disappears from the story  after everything she did for the sins  not cool man  not cool now it is possible that the  sequel manga is planning to cover the  supreme deity and that is why we didn't  get to see her in the original manga  and from the lancelot side story it is  clear that the lady of the lake  is definitely going to be relevant to  the sequel so maybe the same will be the  case  for the supreme deity if that's true  then fine  but that doesn't change the fact that  the original manga ended with  kath as the final major villain and that  was just  underwhelming in my opinion so for me  personally the biggest  issues with the ending were merlin's  true intentions and her flimsy  justifications for wanting to resurrect  chaos even at the cost of putting her  friends in danger  and the ignoring of the supreme deity  while elevating a side character like  kath palug into the final villain in the  story  if i could change the story in any way  that i wanted i definitely would have  expanded the chaos arc  included an epic final battle against  the supreme deity  and i would have fleshed out merlin's  true intentions more thoroughly  but those are just my own thoughts on  the ending and i've been thinking about  this stuff ever since the manga came to  a conclusion many months ago  now let's see how you guys thought the  series should have ended over on twitter  and instagram and of course if you want  to be featured in future videos like  this one don't forget to follow me  at anime uproar over on twitter there  were a lot of comments about lord twigo  and how he should have been revealed as  the mastermind behind the entire story  even nox taku got in on the action  because  of course he did but little do these  commenters know that lord tuigo's true  purpose  stretches far beyond the scope of the  seven deadly sins manga  he is clearly a trans-dimensional and  multiversal entity  and any attempt to understand his true  intentions and motivations through the  lands of the seven deadly sins alone  is absolutely futile you should know  that by now knux  come on man we also had comments like  this one from vtsukuya about the need to  explore chaos power  in greater detail and also the need to  bring the supreme deity into the story  as the final villain  i mentioned these points in the video as  well so i totally agree  with this sentiment we had comments like  this one from juan mas suggesting that  the entire king of chaos arc was  unnecessary i agree that this arc felt  rushed and incomplete  but if we didn't have this arc at all  then we would still have a lot of  unsolved mysteries  unanswered questions and incomplete  segments of the story for example  merlin's true motivations would not have  been revealed at all  and we would still be wondering about a  lot of things like chaos  hawks mama and of course the supreme  deity although the chaos arc didn't  actually help us when it comes to the  supreme deity  my take is that the chaos arc should  have been included but it should have  been expanded  or maybe an extra arc should have been  added that dealt with the supreme deity  shu chiha echoes the idea that we needed  to learn more about merlin and the  supreme deity and  hsk points out that it would have been  cool to see the celestial realm  and to learn more about hawk's mama i  have to agree on these points as well  we might still get more about this stuff  in the sequel but i think it would have  been better to include it in the main  story  over on instagram we also had a number  of comments saying that the supreme  deity should have been the final villain  like this one from luffy king 355 we had  multiple comments saying that esquinor  should not have died or that he should  have been revived  such as these comments by taki xtaki  benny reds and  nate nightingale there were also some  comments like this one by lame head park  beth about the possibility of the  supreme deity being involved  in the sequel and i think that's  definitely possible  but i still agree with the people who  wanted to see the supreme deity as the  final villain in the original story  nevertheless i am excited for the sequel  and i will definitely give it a chance  huge thanks to everyone who gave their  input on twitter and instagram  and feel free to let me know what you  guys think down in the comments below  how do you guys think that the seven  deadly sins manga should have ended  were there any issues that particularly  rubbed you the wrong way  and what would you like to see in the  sequel let me know  down below if you enjoyed this video and  you want to see more seven deadly synths  content and sequel content right here on  the channel  please leave a like to let me know it  really does help and if you happen to be  new to anime opera  or maybe you just haven't subscribed  make this the video that you subscribe  and hit that notification bell to turn  on all notifications  as always thank you guys so much for  watching and until next time  see ya space cowboys  [Music]  you
 

